      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "769 Fed. Appx. 654, vacated and remanded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All told, the two offcers fred 13 shots at Torres, striking her twice in the back and temporarily paralyzing her left arm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted certiorari."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The rule we announce today is narrow. In addition to the requirement of intent to restrain, a seizure by force\u2014absent submission\u2014lasts only as long as the application of force."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Police officers",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The offcers and their amici stress that common law rules are not automatically \u201celevated to constitutional proscriptions,\u201d Hodari D., 499 U. S., at 626, n. 2, especially if they are \u201cdistorted almost beyond recognition when literally applied,\u201d Garner, 471 U. S., at 15."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0001-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We hold that the application of physical force to the body of a person with intent to restrain is a seizure even if the person does not submit and is not subdued."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The judgment of the Court of Appeals is vacated, and the case is remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Torres admits, she was \u201ctripping out bad\u201d on methamphetamine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0002-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The majority's answer to the Constitution's text is to ignore it. The majority stands mute before the consensus among founding-era dictionaries, this Court's early cases interpreting the word \u201cseizure,\u201d and the Warrant Clause. It admits its interpretation spurns the canonical interpretive principle that a single word in a legal text does not change its meaning depending on what object it modifes. All we're offered is a curated snippet and an unhelpful hypothetical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0003-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Once more, the majority's primary answer to all this countervailing evidence is to ignore it. And once more, the majority's own sources do more to hurt than help its cause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0003-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\u201cTo arrest,\u201d Johnson said, was \u201c[t]o seize,\u201d \u201cto detain by power,\u201d \u201c[t]o withhold; to hinder,\u201d and \u201c[t]o stop motion.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0003-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "two years before Hodari D.: \u201cIt is clear, in other words, that a Fourth Amendment seizure\u201d occurs \u201conly when there is a governmental termination of freedom of movement through means intentionally applied.\u201d 489 U. S., at 597 (emphasis deleted)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0004-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Even within its feld of operation, the majority's rule seems destined to underdeliver on its predicted effciencies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0004-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If effciency cannot explain today's decision, what's left?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-292",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4a0e77e7c462b1ca3a9185afa1406677b4e5b28cee2f9fdfc78f5929d4c87f53",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4a0e77e7c462-0004-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "To rule as it does, the majority must endow the term \u201cseizure\u201d with two different meanings at the same time."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
